  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/...\nIssued 318 AM MDT TUE SEP 15 2026\nPrecipitation chances look to decrease across the region on \nFriday, but mountains in central Idaho and northeast Oregon look\nto keep at least a 30-40% chance of showers and a 10-15% chance\nof thunderstorms through Friday night. Southerly flow aloft \nwill keep temperatures near normal through Friday, ahead of \ncooler temperatures on Saturday with the low center moving\nover the region. The low pressure system will then exit to the \neast on Saturday, with showers and cooler temperatures lingering\nover the central Idaho mountains. High pressure will build in \nover the region on Sunday, with temperatures trending slightly \nabove normal (3-5 degrees) on Monday. A cold front associated \nwith a broad upper level trough then looks to move in sometime \non Tuesday, bringing slightly cooler temperatures and a slight \nchance of mountain rain showers.",
